GAL22V10
UA6_crack


AB1  AB2  AB3  AB4  AB5   AB6    STRB   CFG8M   CFG4M   CFG2M   BASEA  GND
RW   CFGIN NC1  ACPHASE  RST    BIN3   BIN2    BIN1    BIN0    NC2    DRVEN  VCC


; ============================================================
;   UA6 GAL22V10 - Original crack from TL866-II black-box sweep
; ============================================================
;
;   Method
;   ------
;   The original UA6 was placed in a TL866-II+ socket and swept
;   through the full 2^14 = 16,384 input space via minipro's
;   --logic_test (two-pass pull-up/pull-down measurement). Every
;   observed output value was captured and cross-checked against
;   every input pattern.
;
;   Result
;   ------
;   Pin 15 (NC1)     - driven LOW  for every input pattern
;   Pin 16 (ACPHASE) - driven LOW  for every input pattern
;   Pins 18-23       - Hi-Z (tri-stated) for every input pattern
;
;   That's it. UA6 is a two-signal pulldown driver.
;
;   Why a GAL for two constant lows?
;   --------------------------------
;   Almost certainly bus contention. A GAL output can sink ~24 mA;
;   a resistor to GND is limited to whatever the pull-up on the
;   opposing net can source. If NC1 or ACPHASE tap into a bus that
;   also has a pull-up somewhere, the resistor route can't win.
;   This is why Draft 11 (do-nothing / all Hi-Z) red-screened -
;   the pull-up won by default and the card mis-behaved.
;
;   BIN0..BIN3, NC2, DRVEN
;   ----------------------
;   All permanently tri-stated. Autoconfig response bytes come
;   from the ROM chain via the 32.7 ohm series resistors on
;   DB12..DB15; UA6 was never the driver. DRVEN never touches
;   UA4 pin 14 - UA4 pin 14 is pulled by something else.
;
; ============================================================


; --- The two active outputs: both hard LOW ------------------
; /output = VCC   means the "not the output" side is always TRUE,
; which means the output itself is always FALSE (LOW).

/NC1     = VCC
/ACPHASE = VCC


; --- The six unused outputs are left with no equation ------
; A macrocell with no equation defaults to Hi-Z on the pin, which
; is exactly what the original UA6 does.  BIN3..BIN0, NC2, DRVEN
; get no equations here on purpose.


DESCRIPTION

UA6 GAL22V10 - original crack.

Pin 15 (NC1)     : driven constant LOW
Pin 16 (ACPHASE) : driven constant LOW
Pins 18-23       : permanently Hi-Z

Verified against a full 2^14 = 16,384-vector black-box sweep of
the original chip on a TL866-II+ using minipro --logic_test with
both pull-up and pull-down passes. Every input pattern produced
the same output word.
